WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.824
The value of red teaming comes from improvement.

2
00:00:02.824 --> 00:00:11.345
Findings should lead to controls, remediation, monitoring, governance updates, and design decisions that reduce risk in the actual system.

3
00:00:11.345 --> 00:00:27.099
Common improvements include better trust boundaries, least privilege for tools, approval gates, output validation, retrieval controls, logging, monitoring, policy checks, training, incident response playbooks, and clearer ownership.

4
00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:35.161
Prompt changes may help guide behavior, but durable mitigations often require architectural and operational controls around the model.

5
00:00:35.161 --> 00:00:40.529
The system should not rely on model instructions as the only boundary for sensitive outcomes.

6
00:00:40.529 --> 00:00:42.844
Remediation should be tracked and retested.

7
00:00:42.844 --> 00:00:53.969
A finding is not truly closed until the team understands the root cause, implements a reasonable fix, verifies the fix, and documents any remaining residual risk.
